If a patient is an older-adult then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk for the patient during an NSAID-use-dose-and-duration-decision.
If a patient has a hypertension then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk for the patient during an NSAID-use-dose-and-duration-decision.
If a patient has a renal-insufficiency then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk for the patient during an NSAID-use-dose-and-duration-decision.
If a patient has a heart-failure then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk for the patient during an NSAID-use-dose-and-duration-decision.
If a patient has a peptic-ulcer-disease-risk then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk for the patient during an NSAID-use-dose-and-duration-decision.
If a patient has a cardiovascular-disease-risk then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk for the patient during an NSAID-use-dose-and-duration-decision.
